# WEIGHTED PULL-UP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Weighted Pull-Up is a vertical pulling exercise performed by lifting the entire body against gravity while carrying additional external load.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer upper-body strength exercises for combat athletes.

It develops pulling strength, grip strength, scapular control and relative strength simultaneously.

---

# Philosophy

Combat athletes spend far more time pulling than pressing.

Grip fighting.

Clinching.

Controlling an opponent.

Breaking posture.

Finishing submissions.

Maintaining control.

The Weighted Pull-Up develops many of these qualities simultaneously.

CAS frequently prioritizes this exercise for grappling athletes and for developing upper-body relative strength.

